00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:42.000
Yeah, so the first question is how, right? How do you do this? And that involves all kind of technical details like training and ordering food on the run. But then the second question, which I think is the much more interesting question, and he says is the much harder question to answer is why. Why would someone possibly put themselves through this much pain? What are you trying to get out of this? And I agree, that's a really interesting question.

19
00:10:42.000 --> 00:11:09.000
What do you think the answer is? Does he know the answer? What Dean would say, I believe, is it's what he needs to do to be the person that he believes he is. And I agree with that. What I think is that Dean is looking for a feeling of pride, right? It's a feeling that doesn't come automatically just because we're succeeding in ways that our society tells us we need to pride, right? It's a feeling that doesn't come automatically just because we're succeeding in ways that our society tells us we need to succeed, right? He was

