The feelings that people describe when they have it are things like, I feel accomplished, I feel productive, I feel a sense of self-worth. That's what authentic pride is. So in some ways, all the things that you're pointing to reflect the fact that when we are doing difficult things, they often require long periods of sacrifice. Can you talk a moment about the role that authentic pride plays in our capacity to work hard toward future goals?

