Now we had this other undergrad who scored high on the words that indicate she'd been feeling a lot of hubristic pride. And what she said was, I found out I got a 4.0 GPA. I obviously found other people to try to tell my score to as many as I could because I wanted to share my success. And I think that's a really nice example because that is what hubristic pride makes people wanna do. It makes us not just think, wow, I feel really good.

